course: dictionary
lesson: 6042
title: What is a meme?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A meme is a funny picture, video or phrase that people copy, change and share quickly on the internet. The context helps you find this meaning. «Memes and comedy can spark curiosity, but you need to know the real story to understand the joke.» The words joke and comedy tell you a meme is meant to be funny.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. «A meme is a funny picture or video with words, called a caption, that gets copied and shared; it cannot explain a whole story.» The sentence tells you the words on a meme are its caption, and that a meme is too small to explain a whole story. Try your meaning in the sentence: "A funny picture that gets copied and shared cannot explain a whole story." That still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Some words are slang, which means informal words that people use with friends. «Connor messages «L + ratio», a meme way of saying «you lost and nobody's on your side».» The sentence explains the slang for you. When the words around a word explain it, use them.
fact: A meme is a funny picture, video or phrase that people copy, change and share quickly on the internet.
fact: A caption is the words added to a picture or video.
fact: «Memes» is the plural, which means more than one meme.
fact: In science, a meme can mean an idea, habit or style that spreads from person to person in a culture.
fact: Memes can be funny, but they can also be unkind or spread false facts, so think before you share.
exercise: Which is the best meaning of «meme» for a pupil? | A school subject about computers | *A funny picture, video or phrase that people copy, change and share quickly online | A kind of online game for two players | A long report that tells the whole story of the news
exercise: «A meme is a funny picture or video with words, called a caption, that gets copied and shared.» What is a caption? | A type of phone | A website for games | *The words added to a picture or video | A sound effect in a video
exercise: Connor messages «L + ratio», a meme way of saying «you lost and nobody's on your side». What does it mean? | You won the game and everyone agrees | *You lost and nobody is on your side | Let's go to the park | Please send me a picture
test: «Politicians use jokes too, and many have social media teams who make memes and videos for them.» What does this tell you a meme can be used for? | *Making jokes or videos that people share online | Hiding the news from people | Writing long school essays | Cooking dinner
test: Which is true about a meme? | A meme is always true | A meme can explain a whole story in full detail | Memes are only found in books | *A meme is a funny picture or video with words, and it cannot explain a whole story
exam: In science, what can the word meme mean? | *An idea, habit or style that spreads from person to person | A type of rock | A number sum | A loud noise
